<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Fabricator.Functions</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Fabricator.Functions</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      Useful global MACROS, shipped as real SQL files rather than C# string literals. A connection-free
      IProvider that hosts no catalog and contributes only DuckDB macros.

      ⚠ IT IS A BUILT-IN PROVIDER ASSEMBLY, NOT A PLUGIN — the same shape as Fabricator.FluidPlugin and for
      the same measured reason: FABRICATOR_PLUGIN_DIR REPLACES the plugin roots rather than extending them
      (PluginPaths.ResolveRoots returns early), so anything shipped as a bundled plugin silently disappears
      for a user who sets that variable to load their own. These macros are documented as available out of
      the box, so they must not depend on a plugin root existing.

      ⚠⚠ IT DEPENDS ON THE FLUID PROVIDER AT CALL TIME, not at load time: every macro here is built on
      fluid_replacement_query. A macro BODY is bound lazily by DuckDB, so registration order does not matter
      and a narrowed FABRICATOR_BACKEND_ASSEMBLY that drops Fabricator.FluidPlugin leaves these macros
      REGISTERED BUT UNCALLABLE — failing at first use with "Table Function with name
      fluid_replacement_query does not exist" rather than at load.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The contract only: no Common, no Bridge. A macro provider marshals nothing. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Fabricator.Abstractions\Fabricator.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- ⚠ The macros are REAL SQL FILES (Macros/*.sql), embedded and loaded by FunctionsProvider.LoadMacros
         — which drift-guards each one (its file name must equal its CREATE MACRO name) and REFUSES an empty
         set. Both guards exist because the DELIVERY path fails quietly: MacroDefinition's own contract says
         a statement that does not parse "is skipped with a warning at load", so a macro that silently did
         not register answers "… does not exist" at the call site, three layers from the cause. -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Macros\*.sql" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
